0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, FEBRUARY 24, 2010\r\rMayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 6:30 p.m. in the Closed Session Conference Room, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer, Washburn.\r Absent: Mayor pro Tem Groveman.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 6:31 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\rInitiation of Litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.9(c): two cases.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015Personnel Matter, pursuant to Government Code, Section 54957:\r PUBLIC EMPLOYEE PERFORMANCE EVALUATION, Title: City Manager.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:00 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 7:05 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer, Washburn.\r Absent: Mayor pro Tem Groveman.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Rubin, Tamuri.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Sparky Cohen.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, City Attorney, reported that the City Council unanimously authorized him to file suit against Los Angeles County with respect to the proposed Mont Calabasas annexation, and that action was taken on the second matter which is required to be reported at this time.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor pro Tem Groveman was absent.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\r Mayor Wolfson introduced the new Captain at the Lost Hills Sheriff�s Station, Captain Joseph Stephen. Councilmember Bozajian announced that Snow Day has been canceled due to weather conditions. The Annual Open House at the Agoura Hills/Calabasas Community Center will be taking place on March 13 and the annual Arbor Day celebration will be happening on March 20. Councilmember Washburn spoke regarding the upcoming visit from a delegation from Anqing China on March 1.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r \r No one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of meeting minutes from February 10, 2010. \r\r Recommendation to award a contract to Advanced Construction and Restoration for traffic signing, striping and marking installation and repair services. \r\r Recommendation to extend the Wildan professional services agreement for an additional six months and increase the contract value by $250,000.00. \r\r Recommendation to approve the sixth amended employment agreement for the City Manager. \r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to approve Consent Items #1, 2, 3, and 4. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor pro Tem Groveman was absent.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1225 to update the Planning Division fee schedule to establish fees for the submission of applications not covered in the existing fee schedule that are newly required by the Development Code; and adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1226 to establish these fees on an interim basis pending the effectiveness of Resolution No. 2010-1225. \r\rMayor Wolfson opened the public hearing.\r\rNo one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rMayor Wolfson closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to adopt Resolution 2010-1225 to update the Planning Division fee schedule to establish fees for the submission of applications not covered in the existing fee schedule that are newly required by the Development Code; and to adopt Resolution 2010-1226 to establish these fees on an interim basis pending the effectiveness of Resolution 2010-1225. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Mayor pro Tem Groveman was absent.\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r \r Discussion of Water Park Concept and feasibility of building such a facility in the City of Calabasas.\r\rJeff Rubin, Community Services Director, presented the staff report.\r\rThe City Council provided direction to staff on the proposed facility.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS\r\r Informational update on code enforcement activities. \r\rRay Soria, Building Inspector, presented the staff report.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of February 1, 2010 to February 10, 2010. \r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r There were no future agenda items.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN\r\rThe City Council adjourned at 8:07 P.M. to their next regular meeting, which will be held on Wednesday, March 10, 2010 at 7:00 P.M.\r\r\r\r\r\r__________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, City Clerk\r\r\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00143\u0015\r02/24/10\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u